<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roussillon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roussillon is a historical region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, at the eastern end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, corresponding mainly to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Pyrénées-Orientales, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpignan">Perpignan</a>. A Carolingian county and later part of the Crown of Aragon and the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a>, it was Catalan in language and culture until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ceded it to France by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-the-pyrenees">Treaty of the Pyrenees</a> in 1659.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roussillon.jpg" alt="Roussillon" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milenioscuro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roussillon_in_France_(1789).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
